        "abstract": "The theory of optimum filtering and prediction is applied to man-machine tracking control systems to improve performance in tracking waveforms which have a somewhat random appearance. The predicted values of the input for a set of prediction times are displayed in perspective for interpretation by the human operator. This display is evaluated in an experimental tracking task.",
